## The persistent session (tmux) of SSH tabs.
tmux-linha = Persistent session
tmux-linha-descricao = With tmux or screen, the tab runs in a session of that program on the server, which stays alive if the connection drops: reconnecting returns to it, with programs still running. Without the program installed on the server, the tab warns and opens the regular shell.
tmux-linha-descricao-pasta = The persistent session of the SSH connections in this folder that did not choose otherwise.
tmux-nenhuma = None
tmux-tmux = tmux
tmux-screen = screen
tmux-herdar-de = Inherit ({ $nome }: { $valor })
tmux-herdar-nenhuma = Inherit (None)
tmux-sem-programa = [Tirech Omni] { $programa } is not installed on this server: the tab opened the regular shell, without a persistent session.
tmux-fechar-titulo = End the session on the server?
tmux-fechar-texto = The { $conexao } tab was running in { $programa } session { $sessao }, which is still alive on the server. Ending the session closes the programs running in it; keeping it leaves the session for next time.
tmux-fechar-encerrar = End the session
tmux-fechar-manter = Keep on the server
tmux-fechar-lembrar = Remember my choice (change it in Settings › Connections)
tmux-fechar-texto-varias = { $n } tabs were running in persistent sessions ({ $lista }), which are still alive on the server. Ending the sessions closes the programs running in them; keeping them leaves the sessions for next time.

mouse-linha = Mouse in the terminal
mouse-linha-descricao = Copy and paste: selecting copies and the right button copies (with a selection) or pastes (without); Ctrl+right-click opens the menu. Menu: the right button opens the menu and selecting doesn't copy. Inherit follows the folder and, with no folder choosing, Settings › Terminal.
mouse-linha-descricao-pasta = The mouse in the terminal for the connections in this folder that didn't choose something else.
mouse-copiar-colar = Copy and paste
mouse-menu = Menu
mouse-herdar-de = Inherit ({ $nome })
mouse-herdar-configuracoes = Inherit (Settings)
retentar-linha = Retry after
retentar-linha-descricao = When the connection reconnects automatically and the attempts run out, waits this long and starts another round, until the connection is back. Off: stops after the attempts. Applies with Settings › Connections › When the connection drops set to Reconnect automatically, and to an assistant's tab. Inherit follows the folder and, with no folder choosing, Settings.
retentar-linha-descricao-pasta = For the connections in this folder that didn't choose something else: how long to wait, after the automatic reconnect attempts, before starting another round.
retentar-desligado = Off
retentar-minutos = { $n } min
retentar-horas = { $n } h
retentar-herdar-de = Inherit ({ $nome })
retentar-herdar-configuracoes = Inherit (Settings)
ocioso-linha = Close idle after
ocioso-linha-descricao = Closes this connection's tab after this long with nothing typed, pasted or sent by an assistant. Output from the server doesn't count as use. A persistent session (tmux or screen) stays on the server. Inherit follows the folder and, with no folder choosing, Settings › Connections, where it's off.
ocioso-linha-descricao-pasta = For the connections in this folder that didn't choose something else: how long without use before the tab closes on its own.
ocioso-fechou = The tab { $aba } closed after { $tempo } without use.

